            {
                "entry_id": "37b26319-0665-3bbe-b1c2-42605506c680",
                "word": "bede",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5d5cf0fd-e096-4aaa-9d1c-35cdacd7aba0",
                        "entry_id": "37b26319-0665-3bbe-b1c2-42605506c680",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bedes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "236f2d7e-059d-34a7-aa1b-1b5ee531cac0",
                        "entry_id": "37b26319-0665-3bbe-b1c2-42605506c680",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prayer, request, supplication"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14b97fe7-3af2-4f01-8f5f-8d5bee48d884",
                                "sense_id": "236f2d7e-059d-34a7-aa1b-1b5ee531cac0",
                                "text": "[…] because miracles had frequently been done at his burial-place, even at the bede-house where he was buried."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81c5fb96-2bff-427b-a9db-f29d02eed8ce",
                                "sense_id": "236f2d7e-059d-34a7-aa1b-1b5ee531cac0",
                                "text": "Thus originated the alms-(or bede-) houses so frequently met with in the retired villages of England."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be6168ed-1e12-4216-baa9-f7c169f5e227",
                                "sense_id": "236f2d7e-059d-34a7-aa1b-1b5ee531cac0",
                                "text": "By Allah thy bede is good indeed and right is thy rede!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2ae1832-2153-4747-93ed-98adbb336970",
                                "sense_id": "236f2d7e-059d-34a7-aa1b-1b5ee531cac0",
                                "text": "Because of the length of the original rosary, it became customary to pay someone, usually a resident of an almshouse, to recite the prayers. These people were referred to as bede women or men, and it was they who made the first bead flowers."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a22041f1-43fa-3862-ad4b-28e14a4c82f8",
                        "entry_id": "37b26319-0665-3bbe-b1c2-42605506c680",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rosary."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76210995-84a4-493a-9688-d1ed558eb976",
                                "sense_id": "a22041f1-43fa-3862-ad4b-28e14a4c82f8",
                                "text": "In Pilgrimage from towne to towne: With offring and with Drilon: To them they bable on their bedes: That they may helpe them in their nedes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d4eae2d-7078-4ef8-96a7-ffe343886796",
                                "sense_id": "a22041f1-43fa-3862-ad4b-28e14a4c82f8",
                                "text": "Or doe they use their Bedes alone to finde That tale of Paters which they seldome minde?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "077c4ff4-0131-40d2-95fe-44e57d0d3a3a",
                                "sense_id": "a22041f1-43fa-3862-ad4b-28e14a4c82f8",
                                "text": "Towards a rude hermitage he made To fetch the priest unto his need, To bury her and say her bede"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e07ab8c2-90a0-4d39-8d2e-c0652376abad",
                                "sense_id": "a22041f1-43fa-3862-ad4b-28e14a4c82f8",
                                "text": "Then the Little Serving Maid She went and laid her down, With her cross and her bede, In her new courting gown."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
